  message: "Fixed by the stable_id v6->v7 scheme bump (merged selfh/dev @ 7577945512). Folded make_file_stable_id(lang, normalize_path(rel_path)) into the containing_stable_id slot of compute_stable_id (untyped) + make_typed_stable_id (typed) at every tree-sitter producer call site across 46 analyzers; py.py was already file-anchored (v4). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: (1) cross-language probe via run_behavior_map — corpus_collision_groups on a Rust/Go/TS/bash sample 1-2 -> 0 (live repro); (2) the filed repro (bash usage() across scripts) is now a passing production-path test, test_wibokab_crossfile_anchor.py::test_bash_same_name_function_distinct_across_files; (3) per-tier cross-file-uniqueness + location-independence tests for bash/ruby/go/rust; (4) full suite 19019 passed / 100% coverage; (5) grammar-independent AST completeness lint proves every producer call threads the anchor. rust.py<->rust_scip.py SCIP byte-parity (WI-zakub) preserved. Residual (opt-in rust-analyzer SCIP doc.relative_path representation + _disk_source_reader CWD gap) split to WI-kilih."  # a00b
